{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>You shall not murder</b> — sixth statement, and it has 6 letters: לו״ך (to you), for man was created on the sixth day. לא תגנוב — in gematria: גונב נפש (kidnapper of a soul). The Ten Commandments begin with alef and end with kaf, and this is אך טוב לישראל. And there are in them תר״ך (620) letters, corresponding to תרי״ג (613) commandments and the seven commandments of the sons of Noah, and their mnemonic is כתר תורה (crown of Torah), to tell you that if a person studies Torah for its own sake, it is a crown for his head, and if he studies not for its own sake, he returns to כרת (excision). And there are in them the number of words of עקב, and this is what Eliezer hinted: בקע משקלו (Genesis 24:22, \"whose weight was a beka\"). ושני צמידים (and two bracelets) — these are the two tablets. עשרה זהב משקלם (\"their weight ten gold\") — these are the Ten Commandments. And this is עקב אשר שמע אברהם בקולי (Genesis 26:5). ובשמרם עקב רב. ואצרנה עקב. עשה תורתך קבע מורשה קהלת יעק״ב — the Ten Commandments, which have in them קע״ב (172) words."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The phrase עשה תורתך קבע מורשה קהלת appears to be a mnemonic string; קהלת יעק״ב likely signals that the word-count קע״ב (172) is attributed to יעקב (Rabbeinu Yakov, the Ba'al HaTurim himself). The references ובשמרם עקב רב and ואצרנה עקב are to verses containing the word עקב (Deut. 7:12 and Deut. 33:23 respectively) but carry no verse addresses in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:50.111794269Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}